  "notes": [
    "Every packet was sealed by the exact producer revision with fixed synthetic key, ephemeral, timestamp, counter, preamble, body, and cookie inputs; independent consumers must rebuild initiator packets and authenticate-open replies.",
    "The producer intentionally echoes the NHP_KNK counter in NHP_COK for relay compatibility, as frozen here, but native UDP consumers must treat the authenticated COK wire counter as unconstrained and correlate only when decrypted trxId equals the originating NHP_KNK counter. The accept_cok_wire_counter_unconstrained flow mutation pins that consumer rule. The NHP_ACK counter must echo NHP_RKN.",
    "The NHP_RKN header MAC authenticates the exact decoded 32-byte cookie after the header prefix and payload ciphertext. NHP_EXT uses the ordinary no-cookie MAC, MUST have no body, and is one-way: the server sends neither NHP_ACK nor NHP_COK.",
    "The successful NHP_ACK carries a nonzero server-assigned uint64 sessId and its resHost, acTokens, and preActions maps contain exactly one entry keyed by the session resId.",
    "NHP_EXT applies to every active access session owned by the authenticated agent identity. It is reserved for whole-agent shutdown, never per-resource stop, replacement-session retirement, or ordinary FRP cleanup.",
    "All identities, hosts, keys, cookies, counters, and tokens are synthetic conformance data."
  ],
